{title: This Is My Song}
{key: C}

{section: Verse 1}
[C]This is my so[Dm]ng, O God[G7] of all the nati[C]ons,
A song of pe[Dm]ace for la[G7]nds a[F]far and mi[C]ne.
This is my h[Am]ome, the cou[Em]ntry where my he[Dm]art is;
Here are my ho[C]pes, my dreams, my [G7]holy s[E]hrine;
[Em]But other hear[Am]ts in other land[G]s are beat[Dm]ing
With hopes and dr[C]eams as true and h[G7]igh as mi[C]ne.

{section: Verse 2}
My country's skies are bluer than the ocean,
And sunlight beams on cloverleaf and pine.
But other lands have sunlight too, and clover,
And skies are everywhere as blue as mine.

{section: Verse 3}
Oh, hear my song, thou God of all the nations,
A song of peace for their land and for mine.
This is my prayer, O Lord of all earth's kingdoms,
Thy kingdom come; on earth thy will be done.

{section: Verse 4}
Let Christ be lifted up till all men serve him,
And hearts united learn to live as one.
Oh, hear my prayer, thou God of all the nations,
Myself I give thee; Let Thy will be done.
